+                                    // process_command returns Ok(hung_up): false for a normal
+                                    // message, true when the peer sent EOF (OkNoData). Peers that
+                                    // exit signal EOF via EPOLLIN (level-triggered) *without*
+                                    // EPOLLHUP, so the old `!ret && event.hung_up` discarded EOF
+                                    // and left dead connections registered -> 100% CPU spin.
